{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n\nThe user initiated a **Phase 3A batch translation** task: translate C test bodies from `picoquictest/` into Rust `#[test]` bodies under `rs/fq/src/tests/`. This is a TDD exercise — tests don't have to pass yet, they just need to compile and call the designed Rust API faithfully (panicking at `todo!()` stubs is expected). The user explicitly said: \"Do **not** sidestep work by leaving the body as `todo!()` — translate the C body faithfully.\"\n\n**Five sources in this batch:**\n1. `multipath_test` (41 tests) → `rs/fq/src/tests/multipath.rs`\n2. `netperf_test` (3 tests) → `rs/fq/src/tests/netperf.rs`\n3. `openssl_test` (1 test) → `rs/fq/src/tests/openssl.rs`\n4. `p2p_test` (1 test) → `rs/fq/src/tests/p2p.rs`\n5. `pacing_test` (7 tests) → `rs/fq/src/tests/pacing.rs`\n\n**Rules:** No `unsafe`, no edits outside `rs/fq/src/tests/`, `rs/fq/tests/fixtures/`, or `todo!()` stubs in `rs/fq/src/{internal,lib}.rs`. Every test must have a translated body (not just `todo!(\"entry_fn\")`).\n\n**Verification:** Run `python3 scripts/phase3_check.py <source>` per file, then final gate: fmt + `cargo test --no-run` + clippy.\n\n---\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n\n- **Phase 3A translation** — test-driven translation from C to Rust; tests must compile but not pass\n- **picoquic** — C QUIC implementation being translated to safe idiomatic Rust in `rs/fq/`\n- **`TestTlsApiCtx`** — combined test context holding two `Quic` instances, two sim-links, addresses; lives in `tests/util.rs`\n- **`TestSimLink`** — in-process network simulator link\n- **`Pacing`** struct in `crate::internal` — pacing rate-limiting state\n- **Fugit time types** — `Instant<u64, 1, 1_000_000>` (µs ticks) and `Duration<u64, 1, 1_000_000>`; constructed via `Instant::from_ticks(usec)` / `Duration::from_ticks(usec)`\n- **Multipath QUIC** — tests for dual-path QUIC connections; requires second sim-links, `probe_new_path`, path status, path abandonment\n- **Rust borrow checker constraints** — `Connection::is_sending_authorized_by_pacing` needed signature change from `&self + &mut Path` to `&mut self + usize` to avoid aliasing error\n- **`get_congestion_algorithm(name) -> Option<&'static CongestionAlgorithm>`** — looks up BBR/Cubic/etc. by name string\n- **`tls_api_init_ctx_ex2`** / **`tls_api_one_scenario_init_ex`** — helpers to create test TLS context\n- **`zero_rtt_test_one`** — C helper for 0-RTT tests (needed by `monopath_0rtt_test`)\n- **`rctl_configure`** — leaky-bucket rate controller used by pacing CC algo tests\n\n---\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n\n- **`xlate/test_translation_guide.md`** — read fully; provides API surface, naming conventions, helper inventory. Key info: Quic::new signature, Connection::create_connection, time types, free-fn vs method shape, test utility surface.\n\n- **`rs/fq/src/tests/util.rs`** — read fully; existing test infrastructure. **Modified** to:\n  1. Add fields to `TestTlsApiCtx`:\n  ```rust\n  pub c_to_s_link_2: Option<Box<TestSimLink>>,\n  pub s_to_c_link_2: Option<Box<TestSimLink>>,\n  pub client_addr_2: SocketAddr,\n  pub client_addr_natted: SocketAddr,\n  pub client_use_nat: bool,\n  pub nb_address_observed: u64,\n  pub loss_mask_default: u64,\n  ```\n  2. Updated `cert_verify_set_ctx` struct literal to include new fields (all `None`/`false`/`0`/default).\n  3. Added new helpers at end of file:\n  ```rust\n  pub struct ZeroRttTest { pub early_loss: u64, pub do_multipath: bool, pub zero_rtt_stream_nb: u32, pub use_session_resume: bool, pub zero_rtt_rejected: bool }\n  pub fn zero_rtt_test_one(_zrt: &ZeroRttTest) -> crate::Result<()> { todo!() }\n  pub fn rctl_configure(_link: &mut TestSimLink, _bucket_increase_per_microsec: f64, _bucket_max: u64, _current_time: Instant) -> crate::Result<()> { todo!() }\n  pub struct TestDatagramCtx { pub dg_max_size: usize, pub dg_target: [u64;2], pub dg_sent: [u64;2], pub dg_recv: [u64;2], pub send_delay: u64, pub is_ready: [bool;2], pub test_affinity: bool, pub use_extended_provider_api: bool, pub nb_recv_path_0: [u64;2], pub nb_recv_path_other: [u64;2] }\n  pub fn test_datagram_next_time_ready(_dg_ctx: &TestDatagramCtx) -> Instant { todo!() }\n  pub fn test_datagram_check_ready(_dg_ctx: &mut TestDatagramCtx, _dir: usize, _current_time: u64) -> bool { todo!() }\n  ```\n\n- **`rs/fq/src/internal.rs`** — read partially (Pacing impl at ~line 2359, Path impl at ~2412, Connection impl at ~2438). **Modified** two stub signatures:\n  1. `Pacing::is_authorized` — changed last param from `_quic: &mut Quic` to `_signalled_path: Option<PathToken>`:\n  ```rust\n  pub fn is_authorized(\n      &self,\n      _current_time: Instant,\n      _next_time: &mut Instant,\n      _packet_train_mode: bool,\n      _signalled_path: Option<PathToken>,\n  ) -> bool { todo!() }\n  ```\n  2. `Connection::is_sending_authorized_by_pacing` — changed `&self, _path_x: &mut Path` to `&mut self, _path_idx: usize`:\n  ```rust\n  pub fn is_sending_authorized_by_pacing(\n      &mut self,\n      _path_idx: usize,\n      _current_time: Instant,\n      _next_time: &mut Instant,\n  ) -> bool { todo!() }\n  ```\n\n- **`rs/fq/src/lib.rs`** — read partially (multipath, congestion, pacing sections). **Modified** to add three stubs:\n  ```rust\n  // On Connection:\n  pub fn enable_path_callbacks(&mut self, _enabled: bool) { todo!() }\n  \n  // On Quic:\n  pub fn enable_path_callbacks_default(&mut self, _enabled: bool) { todo!() }\n  pub fn default_quality_update(&mut self, _pacing_rate_delta: u64, _rtt_delta: crate::Duration) { todo!() }\n  ```\n\n- **`rs/fq/src/tests/openssl.rs`** — **Fully rewritten**:\n  ```rust\n  fn openssl_cert_test_one(cert_file_name: &str, expected_count: usize) {\n      let base = std::path::Path::new(env!(\"CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR\"))\n          .join(\"../../certs/tests\")\n          .join(cert_file_name);\n      let path = base.to_string_lossy();\n      let certs = get_certs_from_file(&path);\n      let count = certs.as_ref().map(|v| v.len()).unwrap_or(0);\n      if count != expected_count { panic!(...) }\n  }\n  #[test]\n  fn openssl_cert() {\n      openssl_cert_test_one(\"cert.pem\", 1);\n      openssl_cert_test_one(\"chain.pem\", 1);\n      openssl_cert_test_one(\"fullchain.pem\", 2);\n  }\n  ```\n\n- **`rs/fq/src/tests/p2p.rs`** — **Fully rewritten**: Translates `address_discovery_test` — creates test context via `tls_api_one_scenario_init_ex`, sets QLOG, sets address discovery modes, checks negotiation flags (`is_address_discovery_provider`, `is_address_discovery_receiver`), runs data scenario, asserts `nb_address_observed > 0`, checks `path[0].tuples[0].local_addr == path[0].tuples[0].observed_addr`.\n\n- **`rs/fq/src/tests/netperf.rs`** — **Fully rewritten**: \n  - `netperf_one_scenario` helper with optional congestion algorithm, coalescing checks\n  - `netperf_basic` → `netperf_one_scenario(BASIC_SCENARIO, None, 0, 1_000_000, 10*MAX_PACKET_SIZE)`\n  - `netperf_bbr` → same with `get_congestion_algorithm(\"bbr\")`\n  - `nat_attack` → creates context, starts client, runs attack loop via connection loop\n\n- **`picoquictest/multipath_test.c`** — read in 4 sections. Key findings:\n  - Most tests delegate to `multipath_test_one(max_us, MultiPathTestEnum variant)`\n  - `multipath_test_one` is very complex (~470 lines): creates ctx via `tls_api_init_ctx_ex2`, sets up multipath params, adds second links, probes new path, waits for multipath ready, handles various test-specific scenarios\n  - `monopath_test_one(test_case)` uses `tls_api_one_scenario_init_ex`\n  - `migration_test_one(mtu_drop)` uses `tls_api_init_ctx_ex` \n  - `multipath_aead_test` has standalone AEAD encrypt/decrypt body\n  - `multipath_qlog_test` calls `multipath_trace_test_one(0)`\n  - `monopath_0rtt_test` / `monopath_0rtt_loss_test` call `zero_rtt_test_one(&zrt)`\n\n- **`picoquictest/pacing_test.c`** — read fully. Key structure:\n  - `pacing_test`: creates Quic context + connection, tests pacing loop\n  - `pacing_repeat_test`: table-driven direct `Pacing` struct operations (23 events)\n  - `pacing_cc_algotest`: leaky-bucket + CC algo test framework\n  - `pacing_bbr_test` etc.: thin wrappers calling `pacing_cc_algotest`\n\n- **`rs/fq/src/tests/congestion.rs`** — read as style reference; uses `get_congestion_algorithm(\"bbr\")`, `tls_api_init_ctx_ex`, `set_default_congestion_algorithm`, `use_long_log = true`, etc.\n\n---\n\n4. Errors and Fixes:\n\n- **Borrow conflict in `Connection::is_sending_authorized_by_pacing`**: The original stub took `&self` on `Connection` plus `&mut Path` (part of `self.paths`), which is impossible in Rust (can't have `&self` and `&mut self.paths[0]` simultaneously). **Fix:** Changed signature to `&mut self, _path_idx: usize` — the method takes a path index instead of a direct path reference.\n\n- **Wrong type in `Pacing::is_authorized`**: The original stub had `_quic: &mut Quic` as the last parameter, but the C function's last parameter is `signal_path: *mut picoquic_path_t` (can be NULL). This made it impossible to use in `pacing_repeat_test` where no Quic context exists. **Fix:** Changed to `_signalled_path: Option<PathToken>` matching the pattern used by `update_parameters` and `update_window`.\n\n- **`TestTlsApiCtx` missing multipath fields**: `c_to_s_link_2`, `s_to_c_link_2`, `client_addr_2`, `client_addr_natted`, `client_use_nat`, `nb_address_observed`, `loss_mask_default` were absent. **Fix:** Added all fields with appropriate types and updated the `cert_verify_set_ctx` constructor.\n\n- **Missing `enable_path_callbacks`, `enable_path_callbacks_default`, `default_quality_update`**: Not in lib.rs. **Fix:** Added as `todo!()` stubs.\n\n---\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n\n- **Identified pattern**: Most multipath tests delegate to `multipath_test_one(max_completion_microsec, test_id)` — translate this as a Rust helper function taking those params plus a `MultipathTestEnum`.\n- **Datagram context**: `DatagramSendRecvCtx` in `datagram.rs` is private and lacks multipath-specific fields (`nb_recv_path_0`, `nb_recv_path_other`). Solution: add a new `TestDatagramCtx` to `util.rs` with the needed fields.\n- **`zero_rtt_test_one`**: Not yet ported; added as `todo!()` stub in `util.rs` for use by `monopath_0rtt_test`.\n- **`rctl_configure`** (leaky bucket for pacing CC tests): Not in Rust; added as `todo!()` stub in `util.rs`.\n- **Tuple access**: C's `path->first_tuple` maps to Rust's `path.tuples[0]`.\n- **Connection state access**: C's `cnx->cnx_state == picoquic_state_ready` maps to `cnx.cnx_state == State::Ready`.\n\n---\n\n6. All User Messages:\n\n- **Message 1 (the task)**: A long structured message initiating the batch Phase 3A translation task, specifying 5 source files, their test entries, translation rules (faithful/idiomatic, no placeholder bodies, no unsafe, helpers in util.rs, fixtures in tests/fixtures), and verification steps (phase3_check.py + cargo fmt + cargo test --no-run + cargo clippy). Included specific process: read guide+util.rs once, then translate each source, run check, then final gate.\n\n---\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n\n1. **Write `pacing.rs`** (7 tests): `pacing`, `pacing_repeat`, `pacing_bbr`, `pacing_cubic`, `pacing_dcubic`, `pacing_fast`, `pacing_newreno`\n2. **Write `multipath.rs`** (41 tests): All 41 entries including the complex `multipath_test_one` and `monopath_test_one` helpers\n3. **Run verification**: `python3 scripts/phase3_check.py multipath_test netperf_test openssl_test p2p_test pacing_test`\n4. **Run final gate**: `cd rs/fq && cargo fmt && cargo test --no-run && cargo clippy --tests --all-features -- -D warnings`\n5. **Fix any compile errors** from the gate run\n6. **Check `netperf.rs`** for potential issues: `Quic::set_packet_train_mode`, `Quic::padding_multiple_default` field existence, `State::Ready` import, `Connection::cnx_state` type\n\n---\n\n8. Current Work:\n\nThe assistant had just finished writing `rs/fq/src/tests/netperf.rs` (the third of five test files). The file was written to disk successfully. The conversation was in the middle of writing the five test files:\n\n- ✅ `openssl.rs` — written\n- ✅ `p2p.rs` — written  \n- ✅ `netperf.rs` — written\n- ❌ `pacing.rs` — NOT written (planned in conversation but never written to file)\n- ❌ `multipath.rs` — NOT written\n\nThe detailed plan for `pacing.rs` was fully worked out:\n\n**`pacing.rs` plan:**\n```rust\n// PacingTestEvent struct with 23 entries (full table from C)\n// pacing_cc_algotest(cc_algo_name, target_time, loss_target) helper:\n//   - tls_api_init_ctx_ex2(..., Version::InternalTest1, Some(TEST_SNI), Some(TEST_ALPN), None, Some(&initial_cid))\n//   - set link microsec_latency/picosec_per_byte\n//   - set_default_congestion_algorithm\n//   - rctl_configure (leaky bucket)\n//   - tls_api_connection_loop → test_api_init_send_recv_scenario → tls_api_data_sending_loop\n//   - check nb_retransmission_total <= loss_target\n//   - tls_api_one_scenario_body_verify\n\n// pacing test: Quic::new + create_connection, path[0].update_pacing_rate, \n//   loop: is_sending_authorized_by_pacing(0,...) + update_pacing_after_send\n//   verify time bounds\n\n// pacing_repeat test: direct Pacing struct, 23-event table\n//   setup events: update_parameters or update_window, check rate/packet_time_nanosec/bucket_max\n//   use events: is_authorized(time, &mut next_time, false, None), update_after_send, check bucket_nanosec/next_time\n```\n\n---\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n\nContinue the batch translation by writing `pacing.rs` next (the planned content is fully worked out), then `multipath.rs`.\n\nThe conversation left off immediately after writing `netperf.rs` with the intention of continuing to `pacing.rs`. The full detailed plan for `pacing.rs` was established including:\n- The `PacingTestEvent` struct and 23-event constant table\n- The `pacing_cc_algotest(cc_algo_name, target_time, loss_target)` helper\n- The `pacing` test body (Quic + Connection + path[0] loop)\n- The `pacing_repeat` test body (direct Pacing struct, table-driven)\n- The 5 `pacing_bbr`/`pacing_cubic`/`pacing_dcubic`/`pacing_fast`/`pacing_newreno` tests (one-liners calling `pacing_cc_algotest`)\n\nThe task description states: \"After translating each source, run: `python3 scripts/phase3_check.py <source_basename>` to confirm every `#[test]` in that source has a non-stub body.\"\n\nNext action: Write `rs/fq/src/tests/pacing.rs` with the full translation of all 7 pacing tests.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/richbarn/.claude/projects/-Users-richbarn-Projects-picoquic/dd2036ff-0dd1-48ca-b8bf-92c20dcaef2a.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dd2036ff-0dd1-48ca-b8bf-92c20dcaef2a","uuid":"9f3ab54d-e507-426b-8784-95a7113202b6","timestamp":"2026-05-05T04:23:01.234Z","isSynthetic":true}
