{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n\nThe user initiated a **Phase 3A batch translation** task (continued from a prior context-exhausted session): translate C test bodies from `picoquictest/` into Rust `#[test]` bodies under `rs/fq/src/tests/`. This is TDD — tests must compile but not necessarily pass (panicking at `todo!()` stubs is expected). The user said \"Do NOT sidestep work by leaving the body as `todo!()` — translate the C body faithfully.\"\n\n**Five sources in this batch:**\n1. `multipath_test` (41 tests) → `rs/fq/src/tests/multipath.rs`\n2. `netperf_test` (3 tests) → `rs/fq/src/tests/netperf.rs`\n3. `openssl_test` (1 test) → `rs/fq/src/tests/openssl.rs`\n4. `p2p_test` (1 test) → `rs/fq/src/tests/p2p.rs`\n5. `pacing_test` (7 tests) → `rs/fq/src/tests/pacing.rs`\n\n**Status from prior session (already complete):**\n- ✅ `openssl.rs` — written\n- ✅ `p2p.rs` — written\n- ✅ `netperf.rs` — written\n\n**Completed this session:**\n- ✅ `pacing.rs` — written\n\n**Still pending:**\n- ❌ `multipath.rs` — NOT written yet\n\n**Verification steps per file**: `python3 scripts/phase3_check.py <source_basename>`, then final gate: `cd rs/fq && cargo fmt && cargo test --no-run && cargo clippy --tests --all-features -- -D warnings`\n\n---\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n\n- **Phase 3A TDD translation** — tests must compile but allowed to panic at `todo!()`\n- **`Pacing` struct** in `crate::internal` — direct pacing rate control state\n- **`fugit` v0.3.9 time types** — `Instant<u64,1,1_000_000>` and `Duration<u64,1,1_000_000>`; these do NOT implement `Default` (confirmed from source), so `Pacing` structs must be initialized explicitly\n- **`Pacing::update_parameters`** — rate+quantum → sets `rate`, `packet_time_nanosec`, `bucket_max`\n- **`Pacing::update_window`** — CWIN+RTT → derives same fields\n- **`Pacing::is_authorized`** — returns bool, writes `next_time` when blocked; takes `Option<PathToken>` (not `&mut Quic`)\n- **`Connection::is_sending_authorized_by_pacing`** — takes `&mut self` + `path_idx: usize` to avoid aliasing\n- **`Path::update_pacing_after_send`**, **`Path::update_pacing_rate`** — on Path (not Connection)\n- **`rctl_configure`** — leaky-bucket rate controller in util.rs (todo stub)\n- **`MultipathTestId` enum** (29 variants) — drives behavior of `multipath_test_one`\n- **`MonopathTestId` enum** (4 variants) — drives `monopath_test_one`\n- **`TestTlsApiCtx`** — has `c_to_s_link_2`, `s_to_c_link_2`, `client_addr_2`, `client_addr_natted`, `client_use_nat`, `nb_address_observed`, `loss_mask_default` fields added in prior session\n- **`PacketKey` trait** in tls.rs — `fn encrypt(&self, packet, header, payload)`, `fn decrypt(...)` — multipath AEAD folded in via path_id XORed into nonce (no separate `aead_encrypt_mp`/`aead_decrypt_mp` in Rust yet)\n- **`PacketContext::Application`** — needed for `queue_misc_frame` call\n- **`PathStatus` enum** — `Available=0`, `Backup=1` — used in `set_path_status`\n- **`tls_api_init_ctx_ex2`** vs `tls_api_init_ctx_ex` — both in util.rs, both take same 4 Rust params\n\n---\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n\n- **`/Users/richbarn/Projects/picoquic/rs/fq/src/tests/pacing.rs`** — **FULLY REWRITTEN** this session.\n  - Contains 7 test functions translating all of `picoquictest/pacing_test.c`\n  - Key sections:\n\n```rust\n// Shared scenario\nconst SCENARIO_PACING: &[TestApiStreamDesc] = &[TestApiStreamDesc {\n    stream_id: 4, previous_stream_id: 0, q_len: 257, r_len: 1_000_000,\n}];\n\n// CC algo helper\nfn pacing_cc_algotest(cc_algo_name: &str, target_time: u64, loss_target: u64) {\n    const LATENCY_TARGET: u64 = 7_500;\n    const BUCKET_INCREASE_PER_MICROSEC: f64 = 1.25;\n    const BUCKET_MAX: u64 = 16 * MAX_PACKET_SIZE as u64;\n    const PICOSEC_PER_BYTE: u64 = (1_000_000u64 * 8) / 100;\n    // ... creates ctx, sets links, configures rctl, runs loop, verifies\n}\n\n// PacingTestEvent struct\nstruct PacingTestEvent {\n    current_time: u64, length: usize, send_mtu: usize, cwin: u64,\n    slow_start: i32, rtt: u64, rate: u64, quantum: u64,\n    expected_ok: bool, expected_packet_nanosec: i64,\n    expected_bucket_nanosec: i64, expected_next_time: u64,\n}\n\n// 23-event table (rows 0-9 are setup, rows 10-22 are use events)\nconst PACING_EVENTS: &[PacingTestEvent] = &[...];\n\n// pacing() test\n#[test]\nfn pacing() {\n    let mut quic = crate::Quic::new(8, None, None, None, None, None, None,\n        [0u8; RESET_SECRET_SIZE], current_time, None, None).expect(\"quic\");\n    let saddr: std::net::SocketAddr = \"127.0.0.1:1000\".parse().unwrap();\n    let cnx = quic.create_connection(\n        ConnectionId::default(), ConnectionId::default(), Some(&saddr),\n        current_time, 0, Some(\"test-sni\"), Some(\"test-alpn\"), true,\n    ).expect(\"cnx\");\n    cnx.paths[0].update_pacing_rate(TEST_BYTE_PER_SEC as f64, TEST_QUANTUM);\n    while nb_sent < NB_TARGET {\n        let mut next_time = current_time + Duration::from_ticks(10_000_000);\n        if cnx.is_sending_authorized_by_pacing(0, current_time, &mut next_time) {\n            nb_sent += 1;\n            let send_mtu = cnx.paths[0].send_mtu;\n            cnx.paths[0].update_pacing_after_send(send_mtu, current_time);\n        } else { current_time = next_time; }\n    }\n}\n\n// pacing_repeat() test\n#[test]\nfn pacing_repeat() {\n    let mut pacing = Pacing {\n        rate: 0,\n        evaluation_time: Instant::from_ticks(0),\n        bucket_max: 0,\n        packet_time_microsec: Duration::from_ticks(0),\n        quantum_max: 0, rate_max: 0, bandwidth_pause: 0,\n        bucket_nanosec: 0, packet_time_nanosec: 0,\n    };\n    for (i, ev) in PACING_EVENTS.iter().enumerate() {\n        if ev.length == 0 {\n            if ev.cwin == 0 { pacing.update_parameters(ev.rate as f64, ev.quantum, ev.send_mtu, Duration::from_ticks(ev.rtt), None); }\n            else { pacing.update_window(ev.slow_start, ev.cwin, ev.send_mtu, Duration::from_ticks(ev.rtt), None); }\n            assert_eq!(pacing.rate, ev.rate, \"event {i}: rate\");\n            assert_eq!(pacing.packet_time_nanosec, ev.expected_packet_nanosec, \"event {i}: packet_time_nanosec\");\n            assert_eq!(pacing.bucket_max, ev.expected_bucket_nanosec, \"event {i}: bucket_max\");\n        } else {\n            let mut next_time = Instant::from_ticks(u64::MAX);\n            let is_ok = pacing.is_authorized(Instant::from_ticks(ev.current_time), &mut next_time, false, None);\n            assert_eq!(is_ok, ev.expected_ok, \"event {i}: is_ok\");\n            if is_ok { pacing.update_after_send(ev.length, ev.send_mtu, Instant::from_ticks(ev.current_time)); }\n            assert_eq!(pacing.bucket_nanosec, ev.expected_bucket_nanosec, \"event {i}: bucket_nanosec\");\n            assert_eq!(next_time.ticks(), ev.expected_next_time, \"event {i}: next_time\");\n        }\n    }\n}\n```\n\n- **`/Users/richbarn/Projects/picoquic/rs/fq/src/tests/multipath.rs`** — NOT yet written; contains 41 `todo!()` stubs. Key test structure:\n  - 41 tests: `migration_controlled`, `migration_mtu_drop`, `monopath_0rtt` (×2), `monopath_0rtt_loss` (×2), `monopath_basic/hole/keep_alive/rotation`, 28 `multipath_*` tests\n  - Most `multipath_*` tests → `multipath_test_one(max_us, MultipathTestId::X)`\n  - `monopath_*` → `monopath_test_one(MonopathTestId::X)`\n  - `monopath_0rtt*` → `zero_rtt_test_one(&zrt)` with `do_multipath=true`\n  - `multipath_aead` → own crypto body with `aead_encrypt_mp`/`aead_decrypt_mp`\n  - `multipath_qlog` → `multipath_trace_test_one(1)` + file compare\n\n- **`/Users/richbarn/Projects/picoquic/rs/fq/src/tests/util.rs`** — Needs new stubs appended after line 976. Key stubs needed:\n  - `multipath_init_params(enable_time_stamp: bool) -> crate::TransportParameters`\n  - `wait_client_migration_done`, `wait_multipath_ready`\n  - `multipath_test_do_keep_alive`, `multipath_init_callbacks`, `multipath_verify_callbacks`\n  - `multipath_init_datagram_ctx`, `multipath_set_datagram_ready`, `multipath_datagram_send_loop`, `multipath_verify_datagram_sent`\n  - `multipath_test_abandon_cycle`, `multipath_verify_all_cid_available`\n  - `multipath_test_add_links`, `multipath_test_kill_links`, `multipath_test_kill_server_links`\n  - `multipath_test_set_unreachable`, `multipath_test_set_reachable`, `multipath_test_unkill_links`\n  - `multipath_test_sat_links`, `multipath_test_perf_links`, `multipath_trace_test_one`\n\n- **`/Users/richbarn/Projects/picoquic/rs/fq/src/lib.rs`** — Needs new stubs appended in Connection/standalone impl (ends at line 2629). Key stubs needed:\n  - `Connection::get_peer_addr(&self) -> std::net::SocketAddr`\n  - `Connection::get_local_addr(&self) -> std::net::SocketAddr`\n  - `Connection::subscribe_to_quality_update_per_path(&mut self, usize, u64, Duration) -> Result<(), Error>`\n  - `Connection::subscribe_new_path_allowed(&mut self) -> Result<bool, Error>`\n  - `pub fn aead_encrypt_mp(out: &mut [u8], input: &[u8], path_id: u64, sequence: u64, aad: &[u8], ctx: &dyn crate::tls::PacketKey) -> usize`\n  - `pub fn aead_decrypt_mp(out: &mut [u8], input: &[u8], path_id: u64, sequence: u64, aad: &[u8], ctx: &dyn crate::tls::PacketKey) -> Option<usize>`\n\n- **`/Users/richbarn/Projects/picoquic/picoquictest/pacing_test.c`** — Read fully; source for pacing.rs translation. Key data:\n  - `pacing_test`: creates Quic(8 conns), Connection, calls `update_pacing_rate`, loops `is_sending_authorized_by_pacing`\n  - `pacing_repeat_test`: 23-event table, alternates setup and use events\n  - `pacing_cc_algotest`: uses `tls_api_init_ctx_ex`, sets link latency/bandwidth, configures `rctl_configure`, runs data loop\n  - 5 CC algo tests: BBR(900000µs, 160 losses), Cubic(900000µs, 210), DCubic(900000µs, 240), FastCC(1000000µs, 180), Newreno(900000µs, 100)\n\n- **`/Users/richbarn/Projects/picoquic/picoquictest/multipath_test.c`** — Read in 5 large sections. Key structure:\n  - `migration_test_one(mtu_drop)` — creates ctx, loops, probes new path, checks address migration\n  - `multipath_test_one(max_us, test_id)` — 470-line mega-helper, controls all 29 multipath scenarios via enum\n  - `monopath_test_one(test_case)` — simpler: init params, set latency, connect, send, verify\n  - `multipath_aead_test` — encrypts/decrypts with 4 path IDs, verifies cross-path decryption fails\n  - `multipath_qlog_test` — calls `multipath_trace_test_one(1)`, compares qlog file\n  - `monopath_0rtt_test`/`monopath_0rtt_loss_test` — use `zero_rtt_test_one`\n\n- **`MultipathTestEnum` values** (C enum, 0-indexed):\n  `Basic(0), DropFirst(1), DropSecond(2), SatPlus(3), Renew(4), Rotation(5), Nat(6), NatChallenge(7), Break1(8), Break2(9), Break3(10), Back0(11), Back1(12), Perf(13), Callback(14), Quality(15), QualityServer(16), StreamAf(17), Abandon(18), Datagram(19), DgAf(20), Backup(21), Standup(22), Tunnel(23), Fail(24), Ab1(25), Discovery(26), KeepAlive(27), JustOne(28), BreakBoth(29)`\n\n---\n\n4. Errors and Fixes:\n\n- **`fugit::Instant` and `fugit::Duration` do not implement `Default`**: Confirmed by checking fugit-0.3.9 source at `~/.cargo/registry/src/index.crates.io-1949cf8c6b5b557f/fugit-0.3.9/src/`. Fix: construct `Pacing` explicitly with all fields zeroed in `pacing_repeat()` test.\n\n- **Cannot add `#[derive(Default)]` to Pacing struct**: Would fail because `evaluation_time: Instant` and `packet_time_microsec: Duration` don't impl Default. Fix: explicit construction.\n\n- **`aead_encrypt_mp`/`aead_decrypt_mp` are \"gone\" in Rust**: The tls_api.rs comment explains they were replaced by the `PacketKey` trait (multipath variant XORs path_id into nonce inside implementor). Fix: add `todo!()` stub free functions in lib.rs with `&dyn PacketKey` parameter.\n\n- **`Connection::nb_paths` doesn't exist**: C uses `cnx->nb_paths` as an integer count, but Rust uses `cnx.p