{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n\nThe session continues Phase 3A TDD translation: translating C test bodies from `picoquictest/` into Rust `#[test]` bodies in `rs/fq/src/tests/`. The rule is \"translate the C body faithfully — do NOT sidestep work by leaving the body as `todo!()`.\" Tests must compile but are allowed to panic at `todo!()` stubs.\n\n**Five sources in this batch:**\n1. `multipath_test` (41 tests) → `rs/fq/src/tests/multipath.rs` — was the only remaining file\n2. `netperf_test`, `openssl_test`, `p2p_test`, `pacing_test` — all done in prior sessions\n\nThe session resumed where the prior context window ended: adding new method stubs to `lib.rs` and `util.rs`, then rewriting `multipath.rs` with full translated bodies.\n\n**Verification steps** (pending): `python3 scripts/phase3_check.py multipath_test netperf_test openssl_test p2p_test pacing_test`, then `cd rs/fq && cargo fmt && cargo test --no-run && cargo clippy --tests --all-features -- -D warnings`\n\n---\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n\n- **Phase 3A TDD approach**: tests must compile; panicking at `todo!()` is acceptable\n- **`MultipathTestId` enum** (`#[repr(u8)]`, 30 variants, Basic=0 through BreakBoth=29): mirrors C `multipath_test_enum_t`; byte[2] of initial CID encodes the test ID\n- **`MonopathTestId` enum** (4 variants: Basic=0, Hole=1, Rotation=2, KeepAlive=3)\n- **`multipath_test_one(max_us, test_id)`**: ~470-line C helper that drives all 28 `multipath_*` test scenarios via the enum\n- **`migration_test_one(mtu_drop)`**: drives `migration_controlled` and `migration_mtu_drop`\n- **`monopath_test_one(test_case)`**: drives all 4 `monopath_basic/hole/rotation/keep_alive` tests\n- **`monopath_0rtt` and `monopath_0rtt_loss`**: listed twice in the C test table — Rust stubs are `monopath_0rtt` + `monopath_0rtt_2`, `monopath_0rtt_loss` + `monopath_0rtt_loss_2`\n- **`multipath_aead_test`**: creates encrypt+decrypt AEAD contexts via `setup_test_aead_context`, then calls `aead_encrypt_mp`/`aead_decrypt_mp` free functions\n- **`multipath_qlog_test`**: calls `multipath_trace_test_one(1)` + file compare via `compare_text_files`\n- **`aead_encrypt_mp` / `aead_decrypt_mp`**: free functions in `lib.rs` (C's `picoquic_aead_encrypt_mp`/`_decrypt_mp` were removed from Rust tls_api but needed as stubs)\n- **`public_random_seed_64`**: seeds deterministic test RNG; free function in `lib.rs`\n- **Borrow checker**: accessing `test_ctx.loss_mask_default` and `&mut test_ctx` simultaneously is illegal — copy loss_mask to local variable first\n- **`todo!()` type `!`**: diverges — all code after it is unreachable; `#[allow(unreachable_code)]` on a block suppresses warnings\n- **`SocketAddr::port()` / `set_port()`**: used for NAT-rebinding address manipulation\n- **`PacketContext::Application`**: used in `queue_misc_frame` call for ping frame\n- **`subscribe_to_quality_update_per_path`**: already existed in lib.rs; takes `unique_path_id: u64`, `pacing_rate_delta: u64`, `rtt_delta: Duration`\n- **`multipath_trace_test_one`**: has `todo!()` for delete+recreate client connection (not yet implementable in Rust); code after it is wrapped in `#[allow(unreachable_code)]` block\n\n---\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n\n- **`/Users/richbarn/Projects/picoquic/rs/fq/src/lib.rs`**\n  - Added ~25 new `Connection` method stubs (before the closing `}` of the last Connection impl block that previously ended with `memlog_init`) and 3 new free functions (after the `impl Quic { nb_data_nodes_in_pool }` block)\n  - New Connection methods (all `todo!()`):\n    - `is_multipath_enabled(&self) -> bool`\n    - `max_path_id_local(&self) -> u64`\n    - `max_path_id_remote(&self) -> u64`\n    - `nb_paths(&self) -> usize`\n    - `path_unique_id(&self, _index: usize) -> u64`\n    - `nb_crypto_key_rotations(&self) -> u64`\n    - `nb_packet_holes_inserted(&self) -> u64`\n    - `renew_connection_id(&mut self, _path_index: usize) -> Result<(), Error>`\n    - `get_peer_addr(&self) -> std::net::SocketAddr`\n    - `get_local_addr(&self) -> std::net::SocketAddr`\n    - `path_is_backup(&self, _index: usize) -> bool`\n    - `path_delivered(&self, _index: usize) -> u64`\n    - `set_path_challenge_required(&mut self, _index: usize, _required: bool)`\n    - `path_local_addr_by_index(&self, _index: usize) -> std::net::SocketAddr`\n    - `path_observed_addr_by_index(&self, _index: usize) -> std::net::SocketAddr`\n    - `path_local_cnxid_path_id(&self, _index: usize) -> u64`\n    - `path_remote_cnxid_sequence(&self, _index: usize) -> u64`\n    - `path_local_cnxid_sequence(&self, _index: usize) -> u64`\n    - `path_peer_addr_by_index(&self, _index: usize) -> std::net::SocketAddr`\n    - `set_local_enable_time_stamp(&mut self, _v: u8)`\n    - `set_local_initial_max_path_id(&mut self, _v: u32)`\n    - `set_local_max_datagram_frame_size(&mut self, _v: u64)`\n    - `set_local_address_discovery_mode(&mut self, _mode: u8)`\n  - New free functions:\n    ```rust\n    pub fn public_random_seed_64(_seed: u64, _reset_context: i32) { todo!() }\n    pub fn aead_encrypt_mp(_out: &mut [u8], _input: &[u8], _path_id: u64, _sequence: u64, _aad: &[u8], _ctx: &dyn crate::tls::PacketKey) -> usize { todo!() }\n    pub fn aead_decrypt_mp(_out: &mut [u8], _input: &[u8], _path_id: u64, _sequence: u64, _aad: &[u8], _ctx: &dyn crate::tls::PacketKey) -> Option<usize> { todo!() }\n    ```\n\n- **`/Users/richbarn/Projects/picoquic/rs/fq/src/tests/util.rs`**\n  - Appended 11 multipath link helper stubs after the existing `test_datagram_check_ready` function (line 976):\n    ```rust\n    pub fn multipath_init_params(_enable_time_stamp: bool) -> TransportParameters { todo!() }\n    pub fn wait_client_migration_done(_test_ctx: &mut TestTlsApiCtx, _simulated_time: &mut Instant) -> crate::Result<()> { todo!() }\n    pub fn wait_multipath_ready(_test_ctx: &mut TestTlsApiCtx, _simulated_time: &mut Instant) -> crate::Result<()> { todo!() }\n    pub fn multipath_test_add_links(_test_ctx: &mut TestTlsApiCtx, _mtu_drop: bool) -> crate::Result<()> { todo!() }\n    pub fn multipath_test_kill_links(_test_ctx: &mut TestTlsApiCtx, _link_id: usize) { todo!() }\n    pub fn multipath_test_kill_server_links(_test_ctx: &mut TestTlsApiCtx, _link_id: usize) { todo!() }\n    pub fn multipath_test_set_unreachable(_test_ctx: &mut TestTlsApiCtx, _link_id: usize) { todo!() }\n    pub fn multipath_test_set_reachable(_test_ctx: &mut TestTlsApiCtx, _link_id: usize) { todo!() }\n    pub fn multipath_test_unkill_links(_test_ctx: &mut TestTlsApiCtx, _link_id: usize, _current_time: Instant) { todo!() }\n    pub fn multipath_test_sat_links(_test_ctx: &mut TestTlsApiCtx, _link_id: usize) { todo!() }\n    pub fn multipath_test_perf_links(_test_ctx: &mut TestTlsApiCtx, _link_id: usize) { todo!() }\n    ```\n\n- **`/Users/richbarn/Projects/picoquic/rs/fq/src/tests/multipath.rs`**\n  - Fully rewritten from 41 `todo!()` stubs to a complete translated file.\n  - **Imports**:\n    ```rust\n    use super::util::{\n        TestApiStreamDesc, TestDatagramCtx, compare_text_files, multipath_init_params,\n        multipath_test_add_links, multipath_test_kill_links, multipath_test_kill_server_links,\n        multipath_test_perf_links, multipath_test_sat_links, multipath_test_set_reachable,\n        multipath_test_set_unreachable, multipath_test_unkill_links, test_api_init_send_recv_scenario,\n        tls_api_connection_loop, tls_api_data_sending_loop, tls_api_init_ctx, tls_api_init_ctx_ex2,\n        tls_api_one_scenario_body_connect, tls_api_one_scenario_body_verify,\n        tls_api_one_scenario_init_ex, tls_api_wait_for_timeout, wait_client_connection_ready,\n        wait_client_migration_done, wait_multipath_ready, ZeroRttTest, zero_rtt_test_one,\n        TEST_ALPN, TEST_SNI,\n    };\n    use crate::internal::Version;\n    use crate::{\n        aead_decrypt_mp, aead_encrypt_mp, public_random_seed_64, AES_128_GCM_SHA256,\n        ConnectionId, GROUP_SECP256R1, Instant, PacketContext, PathStatus, RESET_SECRET_SIZE,\n    };\n    use crate::tls_api::{setup_test_aead_context, LABEL_QUIC_V1_KEY_BASE};\n    ```\n  - **Scenario constants**:\n    ```rust\n    const SCENARIO_MULTIPATH: &[TestApiStreamDesc] = &[\n        TestApiStreamDesc { stream_id: 4, previous_stream_id: 0, q_len: 257, r_len: 1_000_000 },\n        TestApiStreamDesc { stream_id: 8, previous_stream_id: 4, q_len: 257, r_len: 1_000_000 },\n    ];\n    // + SCENARIO_MULTIPATH_LONG (10 streams) + SCENARIO_MULTIPATH_QLOG (2 streams, 10K each)\n    ```\n  - **`MultipathTestId` enum**: 30 variants, `#[repr(u8)]`, Basic=0 through BreakBoth=29\n  - **`MonopathTestId` enum**: 4 variants, Basic=0, Hole=1, Rotation=2, KeepAlive=3\n  - **Private helpers** (all in multipath.rs):\n    - `migration_test_one(mtu_drop: bool)` — full translation including address comparison\n    - `multipath_init_callbacks(test_ctx, test_id) -> Result<()>` — enables path callbacks, subscribes to quality updates\n    - `multipath_verify_callbacks(test_id) -> Result<()>` — `todo!(\"multipath_verify_callbacks: compare CSV output to reference\")`\n    - `multipath_test_abandon_cycle(test_ctx, simulated_time) -> Result<()>` — `todo!()`\n    - `multipath_init_datagram_ctx(test_ctx, dg_ctx)` — `todo!()`\n    - `multipath_set_datagram_ready(test_ctx, dg_ctx, test_id) -> Result<()>` — `todo!()`\n    - `multipath_verify_datagram_sent(dg_ctx, test_id) -> Result<()>` — `todo!()`\n    - `multipath_datagram_send_loop(test_ctx, dg_ctx, loss_mask, simulated_time) -> Result<()>` — `todo!()`\n    - `multipath_test_do_keep_alive(test_ctx, simulated_time) -> Result<()>` — full translation with NAT rebinding and ping loop\n    - `multipath_verify_all_cid_available(cnx: &mut Connection) -> Result<()>` — `todo!(\"traverse remote CID stash\")`\n    - `multipath_trace_test_one(use_qlog_streaming: bool)` — full translation up to `todo!(\"recreate client connection\")` with unreachable code block following\n    - `multipath_test_one(max_completion_microsec, test_id)` — full ~200-line translation with all 30 test_id branches\n    - `monopath_test_one(test_case: MonopathTestId)` — full translation\n  - **41 `#[test]` functions**: all have translated bodies (calling the appropriate helper), NOT `todo!()`\n\n- **`/Users/richbarn/Projects/picoquic/picoquictest/multipath_test.c`** — Read in full (5 passes covering ~2027 lines):\n  - `migration_test_one(mtu_drop)` at lines 256-377\n  - `multipath_test_one(max_us, test_id)` at lines 816-1286\n  - `monopath_test_one(test_case)` at lines 1562-1670\n  - `multipath_aead_test` at lines 1728-1797\n  - `multipath_trace_test_one` at lines 1818-1961\n  - `multipath_qlog_test` at lines 1963-1988\n\n- **`/Users/richbarn/Projects/picoquic/picoquic_t/picoquic_t.c`** — Read to confirm test table entries; confirmed 41 total including `monopath_0rtt` appearing twice (lines 496 and 529) and `monopath_0rtt_loss` appearing twice (lines 497 and 530); NO `multipath_quality_server` entry.\n\n---\n\n4. Errors and Fixes:\n\n- **Potential compile error: `crate::internal::FRAME_TYPE_PING`** — Used in `multipath_test_do_keep_alive` as `[crate::internal::FRAME_TYPE_PING as u8]`. This constant may not exist in `crate::internal`. The C literal is `picoquic_frame_type_ping` which equals `0x01`. This will need to be fixed if `cargo test --no-run` fails. The fix would be to use `[0x01u8]` directly.\n\n- **Potential borrow issue in `multipath_test_one`**: accessing `test_ctx.c_to_s_link.microsec_latency` and then `test_ctx.c_to_s_link.queue_delay_max` requires care. The code extracts `lat` first: `let lat = test_ctx.c_to_s_link.microsec_latency; test_ctx.c_to_s_link.queue_delay_max = 2 * lat;` — this is correct.\n\n- **Cannot pass `&mut test_ctx.loss_mask_default` and `&mut test_ctx` to same function**: Solved by copying: `let mut loss_mask = test_ctx.loss_mask_default;` then passing `&mut loss_mask`.\n\n- **`multipath_trace_test_one` unreachable code after `todo!()`**: Wrapped remaining code in `#[allow(unreachable_code)] { ... }` block.\n\n- **`subscribe_to_quality_update_per_path` signature mismatch**: The C code uses `path_idx = 0` but the Rust method takes `unique_path_id: u64`. Both work by passing `0u64` since path 0 has unique_path_id 0.\n\n---\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n\n- **MultipathTestId placement**: Chose to define both enums in `multipath.rs` rather than `util.rs` to avoid circular imports, since multipath-specific helpers like `multipath_init_callbacks` referencing the enum can stay in the same file.\n\n- **multipath_trace_test_one complexity**: The C function deletes the client connection and recreates it with a specific initial CID (`{8,7,6,5,4,3,2,1}`). In Rust, this isn't straightforward because connections are owned by the `Quic` context and `TestTlsApiCtx::cnx_client()` is itself a `todo!()` stub. Rather than adding a complex `recreate_client_cnx_with_cid` API, the translation includes a `todo!()` at that point, wrapping the remainder of the function in `#[allow(unreachable_code)]` so the code still compiles.\n\n- **`monopath_0rtt_2` and `monopath_0rtt_loss_2`**: Test table has duplicate entries for `monopath_0rtt_test` and `monopath_0rtt_loss_test`. The duplicate Rust stubs (`monopath_0rtt_2`, `monopath_0rtt_loss_2`) are translated as identical bodies to their non-`_2` counterparts.\n\n- **`multipath_verify_callbacks`**: References C file comparison functions not yet fully translated; left as `todo!()` with descriptive message.\n\n- **BreakBoth scenario**: C test expects the connection to fail (inverts the return code). In Rust, the test panics if `tls_api_one_scenario_body_verify` fails. The translation notes this but since `tls_api_one_scenario_body_verify` is itself a `todo!()` stub, the test will panic there anyway.\n\n---\n\n6. All User Messages:\n\n- **Message 1**: \"Continue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with 'I'll continue' or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\"\n\n- **Message 2**: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools... Your task is to create a detailed summary of the conversation so far...\"\n\n---\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n\n1. **Run verification script**: `python3 scripts/phase3_check.py multipath_test netperf_test openssl_test p2p_test pacing_test`\n2. **Run final compilation gate**: `cd rs/fq && cargo fmt && cargo test --no-run && cargo clippy --tests --all-features -- -D warnings`\n3. **Fix compile errors** if any — known potential issue: `crate::internal::FRAME_TYPE_PING` may not exist; fix: use `0x01u8` directly\n4. **Log commands** to `COMMANDS.log` as required by CLAUDE.md\n5. **Update `phase3a_state.json`** to mark `multipath_test` as complete (the phase3_check.py script may handle this)\n\n---\n\n8. Current Work:\n\nImmediately before this summary request, all three file edits had just been completed:\n\n1. **`lib.rs`** was edited to add ~25 new `Connection` method stubs (all `todo!()`) and 3 new free functions (`public_random_seed_64`, `aead_encrypt_mp`, `aead_decrypt_mp`). The edit replaced the section ending with `memlog_init` and the `impl Quic` block through EOF.\n\n2. **`util.rs`** was edited to append 11 multipath link helper stubs after `test_datagram_check_ready` at line 976.\n\n3. **`multipath.rs`** was fully rewritten with:\n   - `SCENARIO_MULTIPATH`, `SCENARIO_MULTIPATH_LONG`, `SCENARIO_MULTIPATH_QLOG` constants\n   - `MultipathTestId` (30 variants) and `MonopathTestId` (4 variants) enums\n   - 13 private helper functions (some fully translated, some `todo!()` stubs)\n   - 41 public `#[test]` functions with translated bodies\n\nAll three edits succeeded (no errors reported). The next